===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# (Also in plural: '''spoils''') [[plunder|Plunder]] taken from an enemy or victim.
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|page=26|passage=Thoſe thouſand horſe shall ſweat with martiall '''ſpoyle'''<br>Of conquered kingdomes, and of Cities ſackt, {{...}}}}
# {{lb|en|archaic}} The act of taking plunder from an enemy or victim; [[spoliation]], [[pillage]], [[rapine]].
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|page=31|passage=This countrey ſwarmes with vile outragious men,<br>That liue by rapine and by lawleſſe '''ſpoile''',<br>Fit ſouldiers for the wicked ''Tamburlaine''.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} Material (such as rock or earth) removed in the course of an [[excavation]], or in [[mining]] or [[dredge|dredging]]. [[tailings|Tailings]]. Such material could be utilised somewhere else.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1961|month=December|title=Planning the London Midland main-line electrification|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=721|text=In view of the decline in freight traffic, it was strange to hear from Mr. Lambert that there is "a continuing problem of supplying, particularly for the civil engineer, the number of wagons required for carrying construction materials and '''spoil''' for various works."}}

